01:14:31.810 --> 01:14:34.000
And you see this number 0.2.

01:14:34.000 --> 01:14:37.240
So earlier, we were always
talking around 1 bits per byte.

01:14:37.240 --> 01:14:41.470
Suddenly, you are getting
0.2 bits, 5x more compressed.

01:14:41.470 --> 01:14:43.240
So this means either two things.

01:14:43.240 --> 01:14:46.930
One, either Sherlock Holmes or
Arthur Conan Doyle's English

01:14:46.930 --> 01:14:50.230
was much simpler than this
modern short story novels

01:14:50.230 --> 01:14:52.480
or something else is going on.

01:14:52.480 --> 01:14:54.340
And any suggestions?

01:14:54.340 --> 01:15:02.350
Why is the compression ratio so
good for this Sherlock Holmes

01:15:02.350 --> 01:15:03.790
thing on the Llama model?

01:15:10.630 --> 01:15:12.478
Do you know how the
