01:16:44.750 --> 01:16:47.420
So it is possible that
for some applications,

01:16:47.420 --> 01:16:49.700
these might actually
be used in the future.

01:16:52.620 --> 01:16:53.120
Yep.

01:16:53.120 --> 01:16:54.100
Yep.

01:16:54.100 --> 01:16:59.540
So something to notice here
is by LLM compressor's work,

01:16:59.540 --> 01:17:01.730
irrespective of how
in machine learning

01:17:01.730 --> 01:17:04.820
you want to be careful
about overfitting.

01:17:04.820 --> 01:17:06.740
For the compression,
say, you come up

01:17:06.740 --> 01:17:09.410
with a model which is really
overfitted on whatever you are

01:17:09.410 --> 01:17:13.175
compressing on and
the model is shared,

01:17:13.175 --> 01:17:14.300
it's actually a good thing.

01:17:14.300 --> 01:17:15.470
It's not a bad thing.

01:17:15.470 --> 01:17:18.800
You might want to overfit and
share that model everywhere

01:17:18.800 --> 01:17:21.710
if you can on
these specific data

01:17:21.710 --> 01:17:24.260
sets you would like to work.

01:17:24.260 --> 01:17:26.510
Why in practice it
becomes a hard thing

01:17:26.510 --> 01:17:29.420
to do because at that point, you
need bigger and bigger models.

01:17:29.420 --> 01:17:31.743
You need higher and
higher frequencies.

01:17:31.743 --> 01:17:33.410
But for compression's
sake, it might not

01:17:33.410 --> 01:17:37.400
be bad to overfit and pre-share
that model on both sides

01:17:37.400 --> 01:17:37.940
if you can.

01:17:37.940 --> 01:17:41.600
That's the context in which
this LLM compressors work.

01:17:41.600 --> 01:17:42.100
Yeah.

01:17:42.100 --> 01:17:42.340
Yeah.

01:17:42.340 --> 01:17:44.800
So Pulkit makes a good point
where for compression, it's

01:17:44.800 --> 01:17:46.480
not necessarily a bad thing.

01:17:46.480 --> 01:17:48.490
If you actually want to
send a Sherlock Holmes

01:17:48.490 --> 01:17:52.030
novel to another person,
compression is good.

01:17:52.030 --> 01:17:54.490
It doesn't hurt you.

01:17:54.490 --> 01:17:56.740
Obviously, if your model is
going to learn everything,

01:17:56.740 --> 01:17:57.948
then the model gets very big.

01:17:57.948 --> 01:18:00.782
So there are issues there but--

01:18:00.782 --> 01:18:02.990
I guess that's why they are
